The change was run against a live streaming server rather than only the unit-test chunks. api.openai.com could not be used (no API credits available), so the endpoint is a local OpenAI-compatible server, Ollama 0.40.9 with `qwen2.5:3b`, called through the `openai` 3.37.0 client with `mlflow.openai.autolog()` on `mlflow` 3.17.3.dev0. The script streams a chat completion (`stream=True`) with a `get_weather` tool and the prompt "What is the weather in Paris and in Rome? Call the tool once for each city.", then prints the output of the recorded span.

Before the change (`main`), the trace loses the tool calls:

```json
{
  "id": "chatcmpl-148",
  "choices": [{
    "finish_reason": "tool_calls",
    "index": 0,
    "message": {"content": "", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null}
  }],
  "model": "qwen2.5:3b",
  "object": "chat.completion"
}
```

With this change, both calls and the finish reason are kept:

```json
{
  "id": "chatcmpl-727",
  "choices": [{
    "finish_reason": "tool_calls",
    "index": 0,
    "message": {
      "content": null,
      "role": "assistant",
      "tool_calls": [
        {"id": "call_y6dgyqzr", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_weather", "arguments": "{\"city\":\"Paris\"}"}},
        {"id": "call_oymwgxrb", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_weather", "arguments": "{\"city\":\"Rome\"}"}}
      ]
    }
  }],
  "model": "qwen2.5:3b",
  "object": "chat.completion"
}
```

(The two runs are separate model calls, so the ids differ.) If you need the run against api.openai.com itself, someone with API credits would have to run the same script with `model=` set to an OpenAI model.
